## Vercel Web Analytics Configuration

**Status:** Already Configured ✅

### Summary
Vercel Web Analytics is already fully installed and configured in this project. No additional changes were needed.

### Current Implementation

**Package Installed:**
- `@vercel/analytics@2.0.1` (already present in package.json)

**Configuration:**
- Location: `app/layout.tsx`
- Import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";` (line 3)
- Component: `<Analytics />` placed in the body element (line 105)

### Implementation Details

The configuration follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router projects:
1. The `@vercel/analytics` package is installed via npm
2. The Analytics component is imported from `@vercel/analytics/next`
3. The component is added to the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`) inside the `<body>` tag

This matches the latest instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

### Files Modified
- `package-lock.json` - Updated after running `npm install` to ensure lock file is current

### Verification
- ✅ Package installed and listed in package.json
